# SSH keys allowed to sign release tags of this fork.
#
# setup/bootstrap.sh refuses to update to a tag that isn't signed by one of
# these keys. The list is read from the version already installed on the box,
# before the new tag is fetched, so a tampered release can't add its own key.
# While this file has no keys, updates only print a warning.
#
# One key per line, in ssh-keygen's allowed-signers format:
#   you@example.com namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
#
# To sign a release:
#   git config gpg.format ssh
#   git config user.signingkey ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
#   git tag -s v78.1 -m v78.1
